\pard{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720 2.0.0.5 Checks the SQLFile Contents. Whe had periodic Problems with CREATE (TRIGGER|FUNCTION|PROCEDURE|PACKAGE) Statements without a trailing Slash (/) on a separate Line after the PL/SQL Block. SQLAgain was hanging in these Situations.\line SQL*Plus requires that Statement to Run the PL/SQL Block which was placed in a Buffer; SQL Developer does not need it. \line We now count above CREATE Statements and the Lines with only a Slash and compares the Numbers. You get a Warning-Message when the Number of Slash-Lines is smaller.\par
